{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-26T19:35:17.299Z","data":{"text":"Task complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented worktree-aware lifecycle commands and the status running-task warning.\n\n**Code changes:**\n- `src/core/lifecycle/reject.ts` — `rejectSpec` now locates the change's `tree` and uses `tree.rejectedDir` / `tree.root`, so a worktree change is moved into the worktree's rejected directory and the checkout is never touched.\n- `src/core/lifecycle/retry.ts` — `retrySpec` recertification runs the task verify via `runVerificationCommand(tree.root, …)` and hashes scope with `computeTaskScopeHash(tree.root, …)`.\n- `src/core/status/status.ts` — `formatStatusOverview` prints the running-task warning directly below the worktree line when a task is running in the worktree.\n\n**Tests:** new `tests/worktree-lifecycle.test.ts` with 4 cases (reject, retry recertification, manual done, running-task warning), each asserting the checkout's change copy is byte-for-byte unchanged. The recertification case proves the verify and scope hash ran in the worktree.\n\n**Verification:** `node --import tsx --test tests/worktree-lifecycle.test.ts` passes (4/4), and the proposal's `pnpm verify` passes (typechecks, build, full suite, lint) after applying biome formatting to the new test.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/093-run-in-worktree/.run/results/4.md`."}}
